#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:14
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A built FHIR Questionnaire shown the way a person will meet it — a mid-fidelity wireframe at web and mobile width, and a live LHC-Forms form view — checked field for field against the L2 wireframe it was derived from, reviewed as a design, staged with deep links, and changed through requests that say which side was edited. Operating skill: fhir-questionnaire-wireframe. WHERE IT SITS. After SUSHI has compiled the Questionnaire to JSON (l3-fhir-pipeline, Task_Sushi), and wherever a layer above reviews a Questionnaire's fidelity to its wireframe. It reads JSON only, so it can run on any IG that produces a Questionnaire. WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM. A faithful Questionnaire is not therefore a good form, and an accepted form is not therefore conformant: wireframe-design-review judges the first and fhir-validation the second."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:68
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A mid-fidelity wireframe with one field per answerable item, each carrying data-element and sitting in a data-layout web or mobile subtree; and the form view, the same JSON in the vendored <lhc-forms> web component on the IG site's form page. Never loaded from a CDN at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:84
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the input: was this Questionnaire derived from an L2 wireframe (a chosen wireframe-design-review candidate)? `yes` runs the fidelity check; `no` goes straight to review."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:131
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by whether a change request (an issue) was opened against this Questionnaire during the review. `no` accepts; `yes` goes to triage."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:148
#. Diagram label
msgid "Apply it to the other side"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:114
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ask for review with deep links"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:123
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "At the deep links. A change is requested through ✍ suggest in its Questionnaire mode, or the questionnaire-change issue form, and says which side was edited: the Questionnaire or the wireframe."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:33
#. Diagram label
msgid "Build pipeline — rendering, screenshots, fidelity"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:41
#. Diagram label
msgid "Business analyst — design review"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "cat-harness Process_WireframeDesignReview: as-is use for a form that exists, design use for one being designed. This process does not restate the method."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "cat-harness Tool wireframe-check: 1280×800 and 390×844; renders, no-overflow and no-placeholder, each a script entry. A rendering missing either viewport does not enter review."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:130
#. Diagram label
msgid "Change requested?"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:89
#. Diagram label
msgid "Check field for field"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:46
#. Diagram label
msgid "Clinical reviewer — the staged form"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:141
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "content-feedback triages the issue; when a review round is open it joins a change-set through public-comment instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:97
#. Diagram label
msgid "Design review"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:23
#. Diagram label
msgid "FHIR modeller"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:90
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "fhir-harness/scripts/check-wireframe-questionnaire.ts <wireframe.html> <Questionnaire.json>, per layout. Exit 0 faithful, 1 a finding, 2 cannot tell, which is never a pass. The findings become the output's fidelity[] and are shown to the reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:136
#. Diagram label
msgid "Form accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:59
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "fsh-generated/resources/Questionnaire-<id>.json, or the IG's published Questionnaire-<id>.json — never FSH. The JSON is what every renderer and reader receives, so it is what is judged."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:11
#. Diagram label
msgid "Is the Questionnaire the form its users and its wireframe need?"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:83
#. Diagram label
msgid "L2 wireframe exists?"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:161
#. Diagram label
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:115
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One deep link per rendered Questionnaire and wireframe, before and after. Where the request goes — the conversation, an issue, the pull request — is a judgement, and more than one may be right: staging-review's deep-link rule, point 5."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:24
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns the Questionnaire end to end: reads the BUILT JSON, draws the wireframe and the form view, asks for review with deep links, triages the change requests that come back and applies each to the side the request did not touch, so the Questionnaire and its L2 wireframe agree again. It is also the only lane with a path back to the start: every accepted change re-enters at Task_Read, so a change is rendered, checked and reviewed exactly as the first version was."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:54
#. Diagram label
msgid "Questionnaire built"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:13
#. Diagram label
msgid "Questionnaire wireframe review"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reached after SUSHI has compiled the Questionnaire to JSON (l3-fhir-pipeline, Task_Sushi), or when a published Questionnaire is reviewed as-is."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:58
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read the built Questionnaire JSON"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads the staged form view and wireframe at the deep links Task_AskReview sent, and judges what the form asks and in what order. The only lane that can send the Questionnaire back: a change is requested through ✍ suggest or the questionnaire-change issue form, on either side, and nothing else re-opens the loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:67
#. Diagram label
msgid "Render the wireframe and the LHC-Forms view"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:122
#. Diagram label
msgid "Review the staged form and wireframe"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:42
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reviews the rendered form as a design against the workflow it serves, through wireframe-design-review: blind, per criterion, at web and mobile width, adjudicated where reviewers disagree. Whether the form lets its user do the task is the business analyst's question, not the modeller's, who drew it."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:75
#. Diagram label
msgid "Screenshots, web and mobile"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:106
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stage the renderings"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:107
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The branch's wireframes and form pages published under branches/<slug>/ by feature-staging."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:34
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The mechanical steps: screenshots at both viewports (wireframe-check), the field-for-field fidelity check against the L2 wireframe when there is one, and the staging build. A fidelity finding does not stop the run here; it travels into the review as evidence, because whether a mismatch is the wireframe's fault or the Questionnaire's is the change request's call, not the checker's."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:137
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The Questionnaire and its wireframe agree and the reviewers raised no change. Conformance is still fhir-validation's to decide."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:149
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The side the request edited is the source of the change. An edited Questionnaire is applied as an FSH edit and the wireframe is redrawn to match; an edited wireframe is kept and the Questionnaire re-derived from it. Then back to Task_Read."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:140
#. Diagram label
msgid "Triage the change request"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/questionnaire-wireframe-review.bpmn:160
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
